# 9. Communications platform by market

## Mexico: practical, expressive, adviser-like

Test content around:

- Daily wear in heat and commuting;
- Breathable complexion;
- Lip and cheek versatility;
- Makeup over sunscreen;
- Acne and post-acne appearance, using compliant language;
- Beginner-friendly routines;
- Shade matching;
- Affordable-premium bundles.

Use native Mexican Spanish. Avoid generic Latin American copy and avoid presenting one idealized Mexican look.

## Colombia: demonstration, consultation, and regional utility

Test:

- Humidity and long-wear performance;
- Differences between cooler high-altitude and warm coastal routines;
- Live product consultations;
- Workday-to-evening application;
- Layering and pilling;
- Community Q&A;
- Professional and micro-creator education.

Do not assume that content successful in Bogotá will automatically work in coastal cities.

## Brazil: native Portuguese, performance, and representation

Prioritize:

- Heat, sweat, and humidity testing;
- Sensory feel and finish;
- Shade depth and undertone;
- Makeup and skincare layering;
- Local creator routines;
- Inclusive casting;
- Product availability and installment convenience;
- Brazilian Portuguese customer support.

Brazilian creative should be created by Portuguese-speaking local teams. Literal translation from Spanish or English is unacceptable for launch-critical messaging.

