# 12. Launch sequence and gates

## Phase 0: Readiness, weeks 0–8

Complete:

- Consumer research;
- Competitive mapping;
- Product and shade testing;
- Regulatory classification;
- Importer and tax structure;
- 3PL selection;
- Marketplace applications;
- Customer-service setup;
- Price waterfall;
- Creator screening;
- Claims library;
- Demand forecast.

**Gate:** No unresolved regulatory, supply, safety, or claims issue.

## Phase 1: Seeding, weeks 9–14

- Seed products to selected creators and testers;
- Build waitlists;
- Publish education rather than aggressive sales content;
- Run landing-page and price tests;
- Test customer service and delivery;
- Collect authentic reviews;
- Validate marketplace listings.

**Gate:** At least 80% of test orders delivered within promise; no unresolved serious safety issue; hero products meet minimum satisfaction and complaint thresholds.

## Phase 2: Soft launch, weeks 15–18

- Sell to waitlist customers and selected cities;
- Limit the number of SKUs;
- Cap paid media;
- Use official marketplace stores only;
- Run controlled affiliate links;
- Measure returns, shade exchanges, contribution, and support contacts.

**Gate:**  
- Owned-site conversion ≥ 2.0%;  
- Marketplace conversion meets category benchmark;  
- First-order contribution margin after variable costs ≥ 20%;  
- Return/refund rate ≤ 8%, with complexion investigated separately;  
- On-time delivery ≥ 95%;  
- No hero SKU stockout;  
- CAC within approved country ceiling.

## Phase 3: Scaled launch, months 5–9

Expand only products and messages meeting:

- CAC payback ≤ 120 days;
- 90-day repeat purchase ≥ 20%;
- Average review rating ≥ 4.3/5;
- Product complaint rate below approved threshold;
- Hero-SKU in-stock rate ≥ 95%;
- Marketplace contribution ≥ 15%;
- No material compliance breach.

Add secondary marketplaces, physical sampling, larger creators, or live commerce only after these gates are satisfied.

## Phase 4: Optimization, months 10–12

- Expand shades only where demand and supply justify it;
- Reallocate paid media toward repeatable products;
- Review owned versus marketplace economics;
- Introduce loyalty or replenishment;
- Test retail trial points;
- Evaluate local packaging or sourcing;
- Reduce or discontinue low-repeat SKUs;
- Set the 2027 country operating plan.

